            <ArticleTitle>Radionuclide imaging in coronary artery disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>79-87</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The utility and limitations of radionuclide imaging in coronary artery disease are presented. Rationale for its usage is discussed in terms of pathophysiologic alterations of the heart and how the pharmacologic properties of these radiopharmaceutical agents can be used advantageously for assessment of such alterations.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
